{
  "_comment": "Field-battle doctrine per culture (#608). Each doctrine is the list of team tactics that culture registers INSTEAD of vanilla's set; the engine still picks the max-weight tactic every 5 s, so a multiplier is a preference, not a script. 'multiplier' scales the tactic's own weight (0 keeps the row but never picks it, 5 is the cap); 'minTactics' is the commander Tactics skill the side needs for the row (vanilla gates at 20 and 50; a doctrine's own tactic should stay at 0); 'side' is any (default), attacker or defender. Charge is always registered even if a doctrine omits it. Reloads on game restart only.",
  "_comment_ids": "Vanilla ids: Charge, FullScaleAttack, DefensiveEngagement, DefensiveLine, DefensiveRing, FrontalCavalryCharge, RangedHarrassmentOffensive, HoldChokePoint, CoordinatedRetreat. TAOM ids: ShieldWall (hold the high ground in a wall, advance in a wall when attacking), InfantryMass (numbers-scaled infantry charge), CavalryDominance (cavalry leads, infantry follows), ArcherRing (infantry ring around the archers, defender only). DefensiveLine, HoldChokePoint and DefensiveRing need TacticalPosition entities in the scene; DefensiveEngagement and ShieldWall use the navmesh high ground and work everywhere.",
  "_comment_culture_ids": "KEYS ARE StringIds, NOT display names. TAOM re-skins the six vanilla cultures via spcultures.xslt, which overrides <name> but NEVER the id: Rohirrim = 'vlandia', Dunlendings = 'empire', Haradrim = 'aserai', Easterlings/Rhun = 'khuzait', Barding/Dale = 'sturgia', Variag/Khand = 'battania'. A doctrine keyed on the LOTR name silently applies to nobody. Cultures without a row use 'default'.",
  "enabled": true,
